# A base constructor may answer with an older object, and `this` behind super() is then that object. A store there is part of the construction of the class that is being constructed and of what lies below it; for an object of any other layout it is a store like any other.
# While the store counted as part of the construction of whatever layout arrived, the literal's field `run` was said to be written at its construction alone, and its closure could have been left unmade.
